\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. King of the city Splendid,
\par Eternal in the height,
\par May all our country's cities
\par Be in thy sight:
\par Cleansed from the deeds of darkess
\par Cities of light
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Teach love to gladden children
\par That know not childhood's mirth,
\par Wronged of their rights-no beauty
\par In their scant reach of earth;
\par To hope's large sunshine give them
\par A second birth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lord end the spell passion,
\par Break thou the drunkard's lure:
\par Thou art the one physician
\par The human heart to cure;
\par The wavering wil to strenhten,
\par Foul life make pure.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Give joy to allthe joyess,
\par Song's voice to sorrows dumb,
\par May light invad with blessings
\par Each dark and deathly slum;
\par Into earth's realm of horror
\par Thy kingdom come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Soon may our country's cities,
\par Thy robe of glory wear;
\par Each place of toll a Temple,
\par Each house a home of prayer;
\par Each cities nam e of beauty-
\par The Lord is there!
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
